  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I've created:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've added a new **`overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)`** function in `src/reports.js` that:\n\n1. **Validates the `asOf` date** \u2014 Returns `fail('DATE_INVALID')` if invalid\n2. **Filters invoices** \u2014 Only includes those with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' whose `dueDate` is before `asOf`\n3. **Calculates metrics** \u2014 For each overdue invoice, returns:\n   - `number` \u2014 invoice number\n   - `customerId` \u2014 customer ID\n   - `dueDate` \u2014 due date\n   - `daysOverdue` \u2014 days past due date (using `daysBetween()`)\n   - `due` \u2014 amount still owed (using `balanceDue()`)\n4. **Sorts results** \u2014 Orders by `daysOverdue` descending (most overdue first)\n\n## Test Coverage\n\nCreated **18 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty invoices and no-overdue scenarios\n- Issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Draft and paid invoice exclusion\n- Correct calculation of `daysOverdue`\n- Proper sorting by days overdue\n- Multiple customers\n- Invalid date handling\n- Edge cases (payment terms NET14/EOM, multiple payments, immutability)\n\n**All 238 tests pass** \u2713",
